/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Content-hashed assets are immutable by construction.
/_assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# There was an /embed/* rule here, framable via an empty `X-Frame-Options:`.
# It is gone, and both halves of it were wrong (D45):
#
#   1. Cloudflare rejects an empty header value outright — it failed the deploy
#      with "Line 16: Invalid header format [code: 100324]", which is how this
#      file was discovered to have never been served by anything. The unset
#      syntax is `! X-Frame-Options`, not a blank value.
#   2. There is no /embed/ route. It came from "charter §14", a document that
#      is not in this repository. Config for a route that 404s is dead weight
#      that fails loudly at deploy time and silently the rest of the time.
#
# If an embeddable widget is built, its headers ship in the same pull request
# as the route, and scripts/check-deploy-config.mjs will require exactly that.
